432 - Shall We Gather at the River
 / 
Key: Db
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 432
Topic: Doctrines - 

Verse 1:
[Db]Shall we gather at the river,
[Ab7]Where bright angel feet have trod,
[Db]With its crystal tide forever
Flowing [Ab]by the [Ab7]throne of [Db]God?
[Gb]Yes, we’ll gather at the [Db]river,
[Ab7]The beautiful, the beautiful [Db]river;
[Gb]Gather with the saints at the [Db]river
That [Ab]flows by the [Ab7]throne of [Db]God.

Refrain:
[Db]Yes, we'll gather at the river,
[Ab7]the beautiful, the beautiful river;
[Db]gather with the saints at the river
[Ab]that flows [Ab7]by the [Db]throne of God.

Verse 2:
[Db]On the margin of the river,
[Ab7]washing up its silver spray,
[Db]we will walk and worship ever,
[Ab]all [Ab7]the happy [Db]golden day.

Verse 3:
[Db]Ere we reach the shining river,
[Ab7]lay we every burden down;
[Db]grace our spirits will deliver,
[Ab]and provide [Ab7]a robe [Db]and crown.

Verse 4:
[Db]Soon we'll reach the shining river,
[Ab7]soon our pilgrimage will cease;
[Db]soon our happy hearts will quiver
[Ab]with [Ab7]the melody [Db]of peace.
